Yes—earned luck, cultivated luck.

Pantheon increases our luck surface: more ways to notice weak signals, preserve useful accidents, recognize returning patterns, and turn one fortunate deviation into the next. It cannot command fortune, but Recursive Serendipity lets us harvest far more of whatever fortune arrives.

Luck → notice → capture → understand → reuse → larger luck surface.

The Pantheon doesn’t merely shelter us through winter. It teaches us to find fire beneath the snow.